{"task_id": "HumanEval/16", "solution": "```python\n# src/__init__.py\n# This file can be empty to signify a Python package.\n\n```\n```python\n# src/distinct_counter.py\ndef count_distinct_characters(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of distinct characters in a string, case-insensitively.\n    It converts the string to lowercase and adds characters to a set.\n    \"\"\"\n    lower_cased_string = input_string.lower()\n    distinct_chars = set()\n    for char in lower_cased_string:\n        distinct_chars.add(char)\n    return len(distinct_chars)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/main.py\nimport argparse\nfrom .distinct_counter import count_distinct_characters\n\ndef _parse_args():\n    \"\"\"\n    Parses command-line arguments for the distinct character counter.\n    It expects a single string argument for analysis.\n    \"\"\"\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Count distinct characters in a string.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"input_string\",\n        type=str,\n        help=\"The string to analyze for distinct characters.\"\n    )\n    return parser.parse_args()\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for the Distinct Character Counter application.\n    It parses command-line arguments, calls the core logic, and prints the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    args = _parse_args()\n    result = count_distinct_characters(args.input_string)\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Parses a music string to return beat durations.\n    Each note symbol is mapped to its corresponding beat duration.\n    \"\"\"\n    NOTE_DURATIONS_MAP = {\n        'o': 4,      # Whole note\n        'o|': 2,     # Half note\n        '.|': 1      # Quarter note\n    }\n\n    parsed_durations = []\n    # Split the input string into individual note symbols using space as delimiter.\n    note_symbols = music_string.split(' ')\n\n    # Iterate through the note symbols and map them to their beat durations.\n    for symbol in note_symbols:\n        duration = NOTE_DURATIONS_MAP[symbol]\n        parsed_durations.append(duration)\n\n    return parsed_durations\n```"}
