{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\n    This implementation efficiently checks for primality by handling edge cases and using an optimized loop up to the square root of n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    limit = math.isqrt(n)\n    for divisor in range(3, limit + 1, 2):\n        if n % divisor == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
